  "limits": "Coverage and overlap use rasterized control-UV polygon interiors, eroded by a 3x3 minimum filter to exclude shared-edge pixel aliases; faces below 4 pixels or with no surviving interior are skipped. This is not proof against every evaluated-bevel UV fold or mip artifact. Images are inspected in rendered close-ups as well. Coverage acceptance uses evaluated UV-triangle interiors because bevels remove unused corners of control polygons; both control and evaluated fractions are retained. Zero-area generated UV triangles and subpixel triangles are recorded separately. This does not certify every mip level or collapsed bevel UV."
